<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  A drawing shape anchored in a Calc cell is in the drawing layer, not in the cell.

  ODF anchors a cell-fastened object by containment: the draw:custom-shape is a child of the
  table:table-cell it is fastened to (sc/source/filter/xml/xmlexprt.cxx, WriteShapes), which is
  what makes its paragraphs look like the cell's. Calc never reads them that way — a drawing
  object is an SdrObject on the sheet's draw page and ScColumn::GetOptimalHeight walks the
  column's own cell storage (sc/source/core/data/column2.cxx:894-949) — so the shape neither
  makes its row taller nor spills into the cells beside it, and it is printed by
  PrintDrawingLayer instead.

  Row 2 holds one such text box: five paragraphs, one of them empty, in a 2.5 x 1 inch shape
  anchored in B2. Rows 1, 3 and 4 hold one short string each and nothing else, so the pitch
  between their baselines is the height an unmeasured row takes.

  LibreOffice 26.2.4.2's own PDF of this file, read with PyMuPDF:

    cells        row 1 "one"    baseline 66.388     the four are a flat 12.784 pt apart, so
                 row 2 "two"             79.173     the text box costs row 2 nothing at all
                 row 3 "three"           91.957
                 row 4 "four"           104.741

    the shape    "Small seven point line"    x 184.507  y  82.943   7.00 pt LiberationSerif
                 "Bold eleven point line"      184.507     94.423  11.00 pt LiberationSans-Bold
                 "Inherits   theshape"         184.507    115.229  11.99 pt LiberationSerif
                 "Last"                        184.507    124.045   7.00 pt LiberationSerif

  Five things a reader has to get right are in those eight numbers.

  The insets are the graphic style's fo:padding-*, exactly: column A is 4 cm and the page margin
  2 cm, so cell B2's left edge is 170.079, the shape's svg:x adds 0.1in and fo:padding-left adds
  another, giving 184.479 against the reference's 184.507.

  A run's face and size come from its own text:span and nothing else. The third paragraph names
  no style at all and is drawn at 11.99 pt in Liberation Serif — the EditEngine pool's 12 pt and
  DefaultFontType::LATIN_TEXT — although the graphic style states fo:font-size="18pt" and
  draw:text-style-name names a paragraph style. Removing the 18 pt, changing it to 8 pt, putting
  fo:font-size="14pt" on P1 and removing draw:text-style-name outright all leave this rendering
  identical; naming P1 on the paragraph itself moves that line to x 223.058, centred. So on a
  Calc sheet neither of those two styles reaches a run, and the control that says the file is
  not simply being ignored is that same P1.

  draw:textarea-horizontal-align="center" moves all four lines to x 210.472 and
  draw:textarea-vertical-align="bottom" moves all four down 15.959 pt, so both are honoured.

  A text:tab draws no glyph and is absent from the reference's text layer: character by character,
  "the" ends at 244.642 and "shape" begins at 245.735, so all it costs is 1.09 pt of advance. The
  three spaces of text:s are in the ink. A span stating fo:font-size="50%" inside a paragraph
  style stating 14 pt is drawn at 14 pt, not at 7 — a proportion is of the parent *style*, and an
  automatic style has no parent.

  The empty third paragraph is 7 pt — its own empty text:span's — rather than the shape's.
-->
<office:document xmlns:office="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:office:1.0"
 xmlns:style="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:style:1.0"
 xmlns:text="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:text:1.0"
 xmlns:table="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:table:1.0"
 xmlns:draw="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:drawing:1.0"
 xmlns:fo="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:xsl-fo-compatible:1.0"
 xmlns:svg="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:svg-compatible:1.0"
 office:version="1.3" office:mimetype="application/vnd.oasis.opendocument.spreadsheet">
 <office:automatic-styles>
  <style:style style:name="co1" style:family="table-column">
   <style:table-column-properties style:column-width="4cm"/>
  </style:style>
  <style:style style:name="ro1" style:family="table-row">
   <style:table-row-properties style:use-optimal-row-height="true"/>
  </style:style>
  <style:style style:name="gr1" style:family="graphic" style:parent-style-name="Default">
   <style:graphic-properties draw:stroke="none" draw:fill="none"
    draw:textarea-horizontal-align="justify" draw:textarea-vertical-align="top"
    draw:auto-grow-height="false" fo:wrap-option="wrap" style:overflow-behavior="clip"
    fo:padding-top="0.05in" fo:padding-bottom="0.05in"
    fo:padding-left="0.1in" fo:padding-right="0.1in"/>
   <style:text-properties fo:font-size="18pt"/>
  </style:style>
  <style:style style:name="P1" style:family="paragraph">
   <style:paragraph-properties fo:text-align="center"/>
  </style:style>
  <style:style style:name="T1" style:family="text">
   <style:text-properties fo:font-family="Liberation Serif" fo:font-size="7pt"/>
  </style:style>
  <style:style style:name="T2" style:family="text">
   <style:text-properties fo:font-family="Liberation Sans" fo:font-size="11pt"
    fo:font-weight="bold"/>
  </style:style>
  <style:page-layout style:name="pm1">
   <style:page-layout-properties fo:page-width="21cm" fo:page-height="29.7cm"
    fo:margin-left="2cm" fo:margin-right="2cm" fo:margin-top="2cm" fo:margin-bottom="2cm"
    style:print-orientation="portrait"/>
  </style:page-layout>
 </office:automatic-styles>
 <office:master-styles>
  <style:master-page style:name="Default" style:page-layout-name="pm1"/>
 </office:master-styles>
 <office:body>
  <office:spreadsheet>
   <table:table table:name="Probe">
    <table:table-column table:style-name="co1" table:number-columns-repeated="2"/>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="ro1">
     <table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>one</text:p></table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="ro1">
     <table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>two</text:p></table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell>
      <draw:custom-shape draw:name="Text Box 1" draw:style-name="gr1"
       draw:text-style-name="P1" svg:width="2.5in" svg:height="1in"
       svg:x="0.1in" svg:y="0.05in">
       <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T1">Small seven point line</text:span></text:p>
       <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T2">Bold eleven point line</text:span></text:p>
       <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T1"/></text:p>
       <text:p>Inherits<text:s text:c="3"/>the<text:tab/>shape</text:p>
       <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T1">Last</text:span></text:p>
       <draw:enhanced-geometry draw:type="ooxml-rect" svg:viewBox="0 0 0 0"
        draw:text-areas="0 0 ?f3 ?f2" draw:enhanced-path="M 0 0 L ?f3 0 ?f3 ?f2 0 ?f2 Z N">
        <draw:equation draw:name="f2" draw:formula="logheight"/>
        <draw:equation draw:name="f3" draw:formula="logwidth"/>
       </draw:enhanced-geometry>
      </draw:custom-shape>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="ro1">
     <table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>three</text:p></table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="ro1">
     <table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>four</text:p></table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
   </table:table>
  </office:spreadsheet>
 </office:body>
</office:document>
